scripts\case-law-information-extraction\output\v1-backup\rules_high_confidence.csv:1261:draftly-rule-courts-coa-ca_dc_479_98.pdf-1,courts-coa-ca_dc_479_98.pdf,,COA,,The plaintiff must indicate whether the property to be partitioned is paraveni or acquired property in the plaint.,In that the Plaintiff has failed to indicate whether the property to be partitioned is paraveni or acquired property.,SRC027-s4,ok-unchecked,verbatim,ratio,high,llm-extract,unverified
scripts\case-law-information-extraction\output\v1-backup\rules_high_confidence.csv:1264:draftly-rule-courts-coa-ca_dc_513_98.pdf-1,courts-coa-ca_dc_513_98.pdf,,COA,,The burden of proof is on the defendant in an action for declaration of title to property where the legal title is in the plaintiff but the property is in the possession of the defendant.,"IN an action for declaration of title to property, where the legal title is in the Plaintiff but the property is in the possession of the Defendant, the burden of proof is on the Defendant - See. Siyaneris vs Jayasinghe Udenis de Silva 52 NLR 289(PC) .",SRC071-s3,none,verbatim,ratio,high,llm-extract,unverified
scripts\case-law-information-extraction\output\v1-backup\rules_high_confidence.csv:1265:draftly-rule-courts-coa-ca_dc_520_2000.pdf-1,courts-coa-ca_dc_520_2000.pdf,,COA,2000,"A party cannot appeal against an order that fixes a date for inquiry under Section 36 of the Partition Law, as there is no confirmed final scheme of partition as yet in the case.",It is only after that stage has been traversed that a party is vested with a right of appeal but of course such party has to seek and obtain leave in the first instance.,SRC027-s36,ok-unchecked,verbatim,ratio,high,llm-extract,unverified
