scripts\case-law-information-extraction\output\rules_high_confidence.csv:1096:draftly-rule-courts-coa-ca-472-97-16.01.19.pdf-1,courts-coa-ca-472-97-16.01.19.pdf,,COA,,"A party claiming prescriptive title must prove undisturbed and uninterrupted possession, independent or adverse to the claimant, for ten years prior to the action.","In order to initiate a prescriptive title, it is necessary to show a change in the nature of the possession and the party claiming prescriptive right should show an ouster.",SRC029-s3,section-not-found,Section 3 of the Prescription Ordinance,True,verbatim,ratio,high,llm-extract,unverified
scripts\case-law-information-extraction\output\rules_high_confidence.csv:1100:draftly-rule-courts-coa-ca-891-2000-f-21.1.2019.pdf-1,courts-coa-ca-891-2000-f-21.1.2019.pdf,,COA,2019,"A partition action can order that any portion of the land representing the share of any particular party only shall be demarcated and separated from the remainder of the land, and can also order that any share remain unallotted.","In terms of section 26(2)(d) of the Partition Law, No. 21 of 1977, as amended, the District Judge, after trial inter alia can “order that any portion of the land representing the share of any particular party only shall be demarcated and separated from the remainder of the land”, and in terms of section 26(2)(g) can “order that any share remain unallotted”.",SRC027-s26(2),bad-source,"section 26(2)(d) of the Partition Law, No. 21 of 1977, as amended",True,verbatim,ratio,high,llm-extract,unverified
