scripts\case-law-information-extraction\output\rules_high_confidence.csv:1144:draftly-rule-courts-coa-ca_dc_853_99.pdf-1,courts-coa-ca_dc_853_99.pdf,,COA,,A party who remains on the record without participating in the trial cannot be considered an aggrieved party.,"A party qua Appellants who missed the opportunity of availing himself of putting forward his case in the original court cannot be treated on par with a victim of an offence who is so desirous of taking advantage of Section 260 of the Code of Criminal Procedure Act, No. 15 of 1979.",SRC027-s25,section-not-found,"Section 25 of the Partition Law, No. 21 of 1977",False,verbatim,ratio,high,llm-extract,unverified
scripts\case-law-information-extraction\output\rules_high_confidence.csv:1145:draftly-rule-courts-coa-ca_dc_955_1996.pdf-1,courts-coa-ca_dc_955_1996.pdf,,COA,1996,"A person who knows the value of the property is not entitled to rescission of the sale merely by reason of the fact that the price at which he has sold it, is less than half its true value.",a person who knows the value of his property is not entitled to recession of the sale merely by reason of the fact that the price at which he had sold the property is less than half its true value .....,SRC029-s101,none,,False,verbatim,ratio,high,llm-extract,unverified
