scripts\case-law-information-extraction\output\rules.csv:545:draftly-rule-commonlii-LKCA-2002-18-3,commonlii-LKCA-2002-18,(2002) 3 Sri LR 343,LKCA,2002,A party may bring a single action to settle all related claims.,(1) The object of the Civil Procedure Code is to prevent civil proceedings from being frustrated by any kind of irregularity or lapse which has not caused prejudice or harm to a party. (2) The two claims urged by the petitioner in the plaint could be tried in law in the same action under section 35 (1) to avoid a multiplicity of actions. (3) The,SRC030-s35(1),none,,,headnote,ratio,high,headnote,unverified
scripts\case-law-information-extraction\output\rules.csv:613:draftly-rule-commonlii-LKCA-2003-12-1,commonlii-LKCA-2003-12,(2003) 2 Sri LR 152,LKCA,2003,A vendor's liability in a contract of sale is limited to providing vacant possession to the purchaser.,"1.��� It is not an implied condition in the contract of sale that a vendor should make a good title, but he must give vacant possession to the purchaser. 153 2. ����� If he fails to do so, if after delivery the purchaser is evicted by superior title the vendor is liable in damages. 3.���� The duty is to warrant against eviction by superior title. Per Amaratunga, J. ""When there is an express covenant in a deed to warrant and defend title and if the purchaser is sued by another party claiming title, the purchas�er should give notice of the action to his vendor to enable him to perform his obligation to defend the purchaser's title. There is no necessity to give notice through court. 4.���� It is desirable therefore that no impediment unless it is absolutely nec�essary should be allowed to stand in the way of his intervening. Per Amaratunga, J. ""When a relevant case is cited to a judge, it is his duty to carefully consider it and decide whether the law laid down in that case is applicable to the case before him; if he decides that, that case has no",SRC030-s18,none,,,headnote,ratio,high,headnote,unverified
scripts\case-law-information-extraction\output\rules.csv:614:draftly-rule-commonlii-LKCA-2003-24-1,commonlii-LKCA-2003-24,(2003) 3 Sri LR 125,LKCA,2003,The main object of appointing a receiver is the preservation and better management of the property.,(i) The main object of appointing a receiver is the preservation and better management of the property. (ii) Plaintiff is not entitled to have a receiver appointed to protect his pecuniary interest. (iii) Order for appointment of a receiver cannot be made upon a consideration of the merits of the substantive claim - that in effect is an,SRC030-s671,none,,,headnote,ratio,high,headnote,unverified
scripts\case-law-information-extraction\output\rules.csv:615:draftly-rule-commonlii-LKCA-2003-24-2,commonlii-LKCA-2003-24,(2003) 3 Sri LR 125,LKCA,2003,A plaintiff is not entitled to have a receiver appointed solely to protect their pecuniary interest.,(i) The main object of appointing a receiver is the preservation and better management of the property. (ii) Plaintiff is not entitled to have a receiver appointed to protect his pecuniary interest. (iii) Order for appointment of a receiver cannot be made upon a consideration of the merits of the substantive claim - that in effect is an,SRC030-s671,none,,,headnote,ratio,high,headnote,unverified
