scripts\case-law-information-extraction\output\rules.csv:836:draftly-rule-commonlii-LKSC-1984-2-1,commonlii-LKSC-1984-2,(1985) 1 Sri LR 35,LKSC,1984,Privity of contract can be established between a tenant and a new owner.,(1) Privity of contract had been established between the tenant (plaintiff) and the new owner (Agnes)' (2) Although the plaintiff failed to seek redress in the partition suit yet the plaintiff was not debarred from invoking the provisions of s. 328 of the Civil Procedure Code. (3) One of the duties of a landlord is to guarantee to the tenant quiet possession of the premises let and a personal bona fide: action the actio conducti (not possessory action) is available to the tenant to claim the use and occupation of the property let and the performance of the duties imposed on the landlord. The action may be brought by the tenant or by any person who succeeds him in his capacity of tenant and it lies against the landlord or any person who succeeds him in his capacity of landlord,SRC030-s328,none,,,headnote,ratio,high,headnote,unverified
