scripts\case-law-information-extraction\output\rules.csv:1067:draftly-rule-courts-coa-1095-99-f.pdf-1,courts-coa-1095-99-f.pdf,,COA,,The burden of proving prescriptive title falls on the defendant where the legal title is in the plaintiff.,"It is settled law that where the legal title is in the plaintiff the burden of proving prescriptive title falls on the defendant (Siyanaris Vs Jayasinghe Udeni De Silva 52 NLR 289, Juliana Hamine Vs. Don Thomas 59 NLR 546, Sirajudeen and two others Vs. Abbas 1994 (2) SLR 365).",SRC071-s3,none,,False,verbatim,ratio,high,llm-extract,unverified
scripts\case-law-information-extraction\output\rules.csv:1070:draftly-rule-courts-coa-27.-judgement-dcf-710-712-99.pdf-1,courts-coa-27.-judgement-dcf-710-712-99.pdf,,COA,,"When a defendant says that the land described in the plaint is only a portion of a larger land or vice versa, the Court has authority to re-issue a commission to another surveyor.","Since the introduction of partition law in this country, when a defendant says that the land described in the plaint is only a portion of a larger land or vice versa, the Court has authority to re-issue a commission to another surveyor.",SRC027-s16,ok,Act No 16 of 1951,True,verbatim,ratio,high,llm-extract,unverified
