scripts\case-law-information-extraction\output\rules.csv:1138:draftly-rule-courts-coa-ca_dc_513_98.pdf-1,courts-coa-ca_dc_513_98.pdf,,COA,,The burden of proof is on the defendant in an action for declaration of title to property where the legal title is in the plaintiff but the property is in the possession of the defendant.,"In an action for declaration of title to property, where the legal title is in the Plaintiff but the property is in the possession of the Defendant, the burden of proof is on the Defendant - See. Siyaneris vs Jayasinghe Udenis de Silva 52 NLR 289(PC) .",SRC071-s3,none,,False,verbatim,ratio,high,llm-extract,unverified
scripts\case-law-information-extraction\output\rules.csv:1139:draftly-rule-courts-coa-ca_dc_561_2000.pdf-1,courts-coa-ca_dc_561_2000.pdf,,COA,2000,"The trial judge must identify the land to be partitioned first, and if the parties are not in agreement about the identity of the corpus and boundaries, it is the duty of the court to identify the correct land.",If the parties are not in agreement about the identity of the corpus and boundaries it is the duty of court to identify the correct land.,SRC030-s44,section-not-found,section 44 of the Civil Procedure Code,True,verbatim,ratio,high,llm-extract,unverified
scripts\case-law-information-extraction\output\rules.csv:1140:draftly-rule-courts-coa-ca_dc_764_99.pdf-1,courts-coa-ca_dc_764_99.pdf,,COA,,A lessee or licensee must first restore the property to their landlord before disputing the title of the person who gave them the lease or license.,In this case the defendant was permitted to occupy the premises with the permission of the Plaintiff. In my opinion the defendant has no defence to this action. He must give up possession to the Plaintiff.,SRC029-s116,section-not-found,section 116 of the Evidence Ordinance,True,verbatim,ratio,high,llm-extract,unverified
